```
  ═══ DISPATCH: COMPILE-TIME (static) vs RUNTIME (instance) ═══

  class FeeCalculator {
     static String version()     { return "BASE"; }   // HIDDEN
     BigDecimal calc(Txn t)      { return t.amt().multiply(BASE); } // OVERRIDDEN
  }
  class SavingsFee extends FeeCalculator {
     static String version()     { return "SAVINGS"; } // hides, not overrides
     @Override BigDecimal calc(Txn t){ return ZERO; }   // true override
  }

  FeeCalculator ref = new SavingsFee();
  ref.calc(t)       → SavingsFee.calc()   // RUNTIME type polymorphic
  ref.version()     → "BASE"              // COMPILE-TIME type (static hiding)
  SavingsFee.version() → "SAVINGS"        // call statics via class name!

  @Override is legal ONLY on instance methods (compiler rejects on static).

  SOLID: LSP — overriding keeps the base contract substitutable.
  Rule: statics belong to the CLASS, instances belong to the OBJECT.
```
